```
labels: top after A | top after B | size after B | top after F | size after F
answer: B | D | 3 | C | 2
wrong[C | D | 3 | C | 2]: A pushes in reverse: C first, then B, so B is on top.
wrong[B | E | 3 | C | 2]: B's list is D, A, E. Reversed, E is pushed first and D last, so D is on top.
